  "body": {
    "id": "lem:district-assembly-soundness",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "If every district task for \\(G^{+}_{Y^{*}}\\) returns a sound factor \\(q_{D^{*}}\\), the Join circuit\n\\(\\sum_{Y^{*}\\setminus Y}\\prod_{D^{*}}q_{D^{*}}\\), with the recorded treatment and context substitutions, equals the normalized target distribution.  If a district returns a failure tag, assembly emits no formula and propagates the least tag.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Y",
      "A",
      "a",
      "H",
      "GN",
      "THN"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:recursive-equations",
      "ass:latent-root-independence",
      "def:elimination-transition",
      "lem:context-construction-soundness",
      "lem:hybrid-kernel-soundness"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Group the finite recursive response-function expansion by the districts of \\(G^{+}_{Y^{*}}\\).  Independent-root factorization places every explicit latent-root probability in the unique district factor containing all of its observed children; deterministic response indicators are grouped with their observed head.  Thus, before summing nonoutcomes,\n\\[\n p\\{Y^{*}(a,s_{\\emptyset})\\}\n =\\prod_{D^{*}\\in\\mathcal D(G^{+}_{Y^{*}})}q_{D^{*}}\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\non the retained parameter image.  The selector/context and hybrid lemmas show that each returned observable factor equals the corresponding factor on the right of (4); compatibility makes its recorded intervention coordinates equal to \\(a\\).  Finite distributivity permits summation over \\(Y^{*}\\setminus Y\\), yielding\n\\[\n \\sum_{Y^{*}\\setminus Y}\\prod_{D^{*}}q_{D^{*}}\n =T_{a,H}^{N}.\n\\]\nThis is the Join circuit.  A missing district factor makes the product undefined, so the case definition correctly emits no formula and deterministically propagates the least failure tag.",
